\label{ex:mukai}
{\em
    Let $G$ be a subgroup of one of the groups in the list by Mukai \cite{Mukai88}, acting faithfully and symplectically on a smooth algebraic K3 surface $S$.
    Consider $p:S \to  \Sigma := S/G$. Since $G$ acts symplectically, any element of $G$ fixes finitely many points, in particular the finite morphism $p$ is quasi--\'etale. The surface $\Sigma$ is thus a normal Gorenstein Calabi--Yau surface, with quotient, hence klt, singularities. Hence, $\Sigma$ has in fact canonical singularities.
